<title>ITALY: Italian crude oil imports rose 0.6 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italian crude oil imports rose 0.6 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian imports of crude oil amounted to some 74.0 million tonnes in 1996, up 0.6 percent from 1995, industry association Unione Petrolifera (UP) said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Libya accounted for 31.1 percent of imports, Iran 17.3 percent, Saudi Arabia 14.3 percent, and the former Soviet Union 12.2 percent.</p>
<p>UP said the cost of imported crude in January, equal to 270,000 lire a tonne, showed an increase of 25.7 percent, due to a 27.1 percent rise in prices in dollar terms and a 1.1 percent depreciation of the U.S. currency against the lira.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
